    "created_at": "2016-03-16T11:53:14Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-03-16T11:53:14Z",
    "body": "So according to [my analysis](http://logs.glob.uno/?c=freenode%23whatwg&s=16+Mar+2016&e=16+Mar+2016#c989349), for `close()` with no argument, WebKit, Chromium and Gecko all send a close frame with no code (the close frame's payload length is 0). In WebKit and Gecko, `e.code` is 1005 and `e.wasClean` is true; in Chromium 1006 and false. (The server's close frame is 0x88 0x00 -- an unmasked no-payload close frame.)\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
